WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
We are now moving into a section that can be emotionally difficult to discuss.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:12.000
Child CPR. A child is defined as someone between the ages of one and puberty. While it is heavy

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.840
to think about, remember that your training is what gives a child the best chance in an emergency.

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:24.400
Most cardiac arrests in children and infants are not caused by heart problems like they are in

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.879
adults. Instead, they are usually respiratory in nature, meaning they stem from a breathing

00:00:30.879 --> 00:00:37.599
emergency like choking, drowning, seizures, or suffocation. Regardless of the cause, once the

00:00:37.599 --> 00:00:43.360
heart stops, the life-saving steps remain very similar to what we have already learned.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.400
Here are the adjusted steps for CPR on a child between the ages of one and eight.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:55.119
One, ensure your scene is safe before you approach. Two, assess the child by tapping

00:00:55.119 --> 00:01:00.240
their shoulders and shouting to check for responsiveness. Look for severe signs like a

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:07.360
lack of consciousness or blue lips and extremities. Three, call for help. Point to someone to call

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:15.199
911 and get an AED. If you are alone, put your phone on speakerphone and start CPR immediately.

00:01:15.199 --> 00:01:20.959
If you don't have a phone and are alone, perform five rounds of CPR first, then go find help.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.919
Four, start CPR beginning with compressions. Because children are smaller, you can use one

00:01:27.919 --> 00:01:33.120
or two arms depending on what is needed to reach the ideal depth. Take a moment to look at the

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.480
images on the screen showing the one-handed and two-handed techniques. Maintain your rhythm of

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:46.080
100 to 120 beats per minute. After 30 compressions, open the airway with a head tilt and chin lift.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.760
Pinch the nose, seal your mouth over theirs, and give two breaths, looking for that clear chest

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:59.440
rise. Continue your 30 to 2 ratio until EMS arrives or the child shows obvious signs of life.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.239
Now please pair up with your partner at your mannequins. We are going to practice these

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:05.440
adjustments together.

